/**
 * @page coding_standards Coding Standards
 * @brief Project coding conventions derived from the 42 norm.
 *
 * ## While-loop convention
 *
 * 42 norm §II.4 forbids `for` loops. A `while` loop must follow the same
 * "split init / condition / update" pattern: initialization on its own line
 * above the `while`, and the update as the last statement inside the loop body.
 *
 * ### Correct
 * @code
 * i = 0;
 * while (i < n)
 * {
 *     // ...
 *     i = i + 1;
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * ### Incorrect (forbidden by 42 norm §II.4)
 * @code
 * while (i++ < n)  // hidden for
 * {
 *     // ...
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * The script @c cub3d/tests/check_while_loops.sh enforces this rule by
 * searching for increment-in-condition anti-patterns.
 */
